== Lua Reference {{dlc|a+}} ==
=== Modding of Isaac ===
The Modding of Isaac hosts an [https://moddingofisaac.com/docs/index.html online copy] of the documentation which has been modified by some community members to be more accurate and easier to understand.

=== Binding of Isaac - Documents ===
[https://github.com/MicroTransactionsMatterToo/Binding_of_Isaac-Documents Binding of Isaac - Documents] is an unofficial documentation project, more detailed than the official one but is far from complete. Online version [https://microtransactionsmattertoo.github.io/Binding_of_Isaac-Documents/index.html here].

=== This wiki ===
Here there is a [[:Category:Lua reference|Lua reference]] category.

== Animation Editors ==
=== Anm2Ed ===
[https://github.com/ShweetsStuff/anm2ed Anm2Ed] is a recreation of the Nicalis .anm2 animation editor, with additional features.

== Room Editors ==
=== Basement Renovator {{dlc|a}} ===
[https://github.com/Basement-Renovator/basement-renovator Basement Renovator] is a tool for editing and creating room files. It can export to stb, the game's binary room format, but saves in xml. Be careful when making Rebirth rooms as some entity ids have changed since then.

== Unpacking ==
=== Rick's Unpacker ===
[https://moddingofisaac.com/help/modding/ Rick's Unpacker] extracts game's files (that will then be manipulated for modding) from .a packed files. If you wish to unpack Afterbirth+'s .a files, it is recommended you use the official unpacker instead.

== LUA Editors {{dlc|a+}} ==
=== Atom ===
[https://atom.io/ Atom] is an open source text editor. [https://atom.io/packages/atom-boilua atom-boilua] is a package dedicated to Binding of Isaac lua modding. (Deprecated project)

=== Sublime Text ===
Sublime Text is a '''commercial''' text editor. [https://github.com/Kapiainen/The-Subliming-Of-Isaac The Subliming of Isaac] is a package for Sublime 2 and 3 dedicated to The Binding of Isaac.

=== ZeroBrane Studio ===
[https://studio.zerobrane.com/ ZeroBrane Studio] is a open source Lua IDE, also mentioned in the [https://moddingofisaac.com/docs/md_input_converted_test__debugging.html official Lua reference]. [https://github.com/Yusyuriv/Afterbirth-API-for-ZeroBrane Afterbirth API for ZeroBrane] is a plugin for autocompletion.

=== Visual Studio Code ===
[https://code.visualstudio.com/ Visual Studio Code] is an IDE for various programming languages, including Lua. [https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=Filloax.isaac-lua-api-vscode Binding of Isaac Lua API] is an extension for autocompletion.

== Code Injection ==
==== BrokenRemote {{dlc|a+}} ====
[https://github.com/MasterQ32/BrokenRemote BrokenRemote] is a code injector with mod examples.

=== isaac-injector {{dlc|na}} ===
[https://github.com/omni-/isaac-injector isaac-injector] is a code injector for Rebirth

== Debugging ==
=== isaac-log {{dlc|na+}} ===
[https://github.com/adewey/isaac-log isaac-log] is a log reader for Rebirth and Afterbirth<ref>Afterbirth+ version planned but never released</ref> written in Node.js.

=== isaac_log ===
[https://github.com/Okiesmokie/isaac_log isaac_log] is a library to read The Binding of Isaac logs.

=== abp-log {{dlc|a+}} ===
[https://github.com/pipe01/abp-log abp-log] is a real-time log reader.

=== isaac-log-viewer {{dlc|r}} ===
[https://github.com/Zamiell/isaac-log-viewer isaac-log-viewer] is a real-time log reader for Repentance.

=== Isaac Debug Helper {{dlc|a+}} ===
[https://github.com/Dogeek/isaac-debug-helper Isaac Debug Helper] aka Isaac Modding Helper Tool is a Python log reader with features like color highlighting and log filtering. There is also [https://github.com/teamdodo/isaac-debug-helper a fork by Team Dodo]. The fork is almost identical to the one by dogeek (indeed the two projects work together) but has an up-to-date release section with executables. When downloading from Dogeek repository, remember to do "Clone or download -> Download zip".

